        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T16:05:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:36.040Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Figure 1: Pull-mode KV transfer timeline, where the router relay, decode-side allocation, and NIXL READ run serially on the path to the first token",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/push-based-kv-transfer-to-improve-ttft-and-tpot-for-disaggregated-inference-in-vllm/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T16:05:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:36.040Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "If you run disaggregated prefill/decode inference with vLLM, push mode can improve application responsiveness by reducing TTFT and TPOT, particularly at high request rates.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/push-based-kv-transfer-to-improve-ttft-and-tpot-for-disaggregated-inference-in-vllm/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T16:05:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:36.040Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In our benchmark on a 1P1D deployment using Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) P5en instances connected with EFA, push mode delivered up to 3x better TTFT and up to 30 percent better time-per-output-token (TPOT) compared to pull mode (see the Performance data section) f…",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/push-based-kv-transfer-to-improve-ttft-and-tpot-for-disaggregated-inference-in-vllm/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T16:05:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-26T16:47:36.040Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This section explains the push-based design: its architecture, the transfer protocol, and the threading model that keeps KV transfer off the critical path.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/push-based-kv-transfer-to-improve-ttft-and-tpot-for-disaggregated-inference-in-vllm/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T16:05:17.000Z",
